{"source":{"wikipedia":"Text and facts from Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 4.0","cfbd":"College stats from CollegeFootballData.com"},"players":[{"slug":"ndamukong-suh","name":"Ndamukong Suh","finalYear":2009,"nflGames":"199","notes":"","signed":"Certified Card","have":true,"wiki":{"title":"Ndamukong Suh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ndamukong_Suh","intro":"Ndamukong Ngwa Suh (born January 6, 1987) is an American former professional football player who played defensive tackle in the National Football League (NFL) for 13 seasons. He played college football for the Nebraska Cornhuskers, earning unanimous All-American honors in 2009. Suh was selected by the Detroit Lions second overall in the 2010 NFL draft. He also played for the Miami Dolphins, Los Angeles Rams, Tampa Bay Buccaneers, and Philadelphia Eagles. Suh played in three Super Bowls during his career: Super Bowl LIII with the Rams, Super Bowl LV with the Buccaneers, and Super Bowl LVII with the Eagles.\n\nAs a college senior, Suh became one of the most decorated players in college football history. He won numerous awards, including the Associated Press College Football Player of the Year Award, Bronko Nagurski Trophy, Chuck Bednarik Award, Lombardi Award, and Outland Trophy.","facts":[],"sections":{"No. 90, 93, 74":[["Position","Defensive tackle"]],"Personal information":[["Born","January 6, 1987\nPortland, Oregon, U.S."],["Listed height","6 ft 4 in (1.93 m)"],["Listed weight","313 lb (142 kg)"]],"Career information":[["High school","Grant (Portland)"],["College","Nebraska (2005–2009)"],["NFL draft","2010: 1st round, 2nd overall pick"]],"Career history":[["Detroit Lions (2010–2014)"],["Miami Dolphins (2015–2017)"],["Los Angeles Rams (2018)"],["Tampa Bay Buccaneers (2019–2021)"],["Philadelphia Eagles (2022)"]],"Awards and highlights":[["Super Bowl champion (LV)"],["NFL Defensive Rookie of the Year (2010)"],["3× First-team All-Pro (2010, 2013, 2014)"],["2× Second-team All-Pro (2012, 2016)"],["5× Pro Bowl (2010, 2012